  "notes": "USAGE:\n{腰掛|こしか}ける means to sit on a raised surface (chair, bench, edge of a bed, etc.). The particle に marks the surface sat on. It differs from {座|すわ}る, which is the general word for sitting and can include sitting on the floor or in any position.\n\nConjugation: ichidan verb ({腰掛|こしか}けない / {腰掛|こしか}けます / {腰掛|こしか}けて).\n\nThe related noun {腰掛|こしか}け means a stool or temporary seat, and figuratively refers to a temporary job or position ({腰掛|こしか}け{仕事|しごと}).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {椅子|いす}に{腰掛|こしか}ける: to sit in a chair\n- ベンチに{腰掛|こしか}ける: to sit on a bench\n- {縁側|えんがわ}に{腰掛|こしか}ける: to sit on the veranda",
